What is printed after serializing and deserializing `UserSession`?

```java
import java.io.*;

class UserSession implements Serializable {
    private static final long serialVersionUID = 1L;
    String username = "alice";
    transient String secretToken = "xyz987";
    transient int pin = 1234;
}

public class SerializationDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        ByteArrayOutputStream baos = new ByteArrayOutputStream();
        try (ObjectOutputStream oos = new ObjectOutputStream(baos)) {
            oos.writeObject(new UserSession());
        }
        try (ObjectInputStream ois = new ObjectInputStream(new ByteArrayInputStream(baos.toByteArray()))) {
            UserSession restored = (UserSession) ois.readObject();
            System.out.println(restored.username + " " + restored.secretToken + " " + restored.pin);
        }
    }
}
```

